{
    "background_story": "McSteamy, a vintage locomotive, once chugged along the scenic railways, carrying passengers through breathtaking landscapes. But after a devastating accident, McSteamy was left severely damaged, its engine silenced, and its carriages scarred. The anguish of being confined to a rusty graveyard, a relic of a bygone era, weighed heavily on the old train's metal heart. As the years passed, McSteamy's paint faded, and its wheels rusted, but the memories of its former glory lingered. The train's anguish was palpable, its stillness a stark contrast to the lively chugging it once knew. Despite efforts to restore it, McSteamy remained a haunting reminder of a tragic past, its anguish a testament to the transience of power and the pain of abandonment.",
